<title>USA: Oregon voters to consider tax reform measure.</title>
<headline>Oregon voters to consider tax reform measure.</headline>
<dateline>SALEM, Ore. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oregonians will go to the polls on Tuesday to vote on a statewide measure that would limit property taxes but require the legislature to replace revenues lost by local schools.</p>
<p>Measure 50 calls for a 17 percent tax cut and a three percent growth cap, similar to Measure 47, which state voters approved last November. State lawmakers introduced Measure 50 after questions were raised about the legality of Measure 47.</p>
